> Original MNIST observations and the shared classifier

The pinned cache contains1000fitting,200validation and200official-test MNIST
images,balanced across all ten digits. Selection seed1931and original source
row IDs are retained in `saliency/manifest.json`;official test IDs are offset60000.
Original28x28bytes becomeFloat32tensors/255. The loader checks all source IDs,
class counts and bytewise duplicate observations across partitions. This small
balanced subset is not the official full training or full test benchmark.

The shared model has26826learned values/eight tensors:5x5SAME8ReLU,VALIDavg2,
3x3SAME16ReLU,VALIDavg2,flatten784,FC32ReLU,linear10head. Convolutions use
HeUniform,dense layers Glorot,biases0,noBN/dropout. Later interpretability
reports restore exactly this selected classifier and its actual initialization.
No method is evaluated on different secretly retrained weights.

Show every one of the200actual held-out images,then retain a deterministic
first occurrence of each digit for the gradient comparison gallery.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vanilla_saliency_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

