> Conclusion

The shared classifier and every local sensitivity remain inspectable through explicit tensor computations,source IDs,finite differences and immutable restored weights. Signed gradients vary with target and actual initialization;they describe local model response rather than causal importance or reliable segmentation.

> References

- [Simonyan,Vedaldi and Zisserman(2013/2014),Deep Inside Convolutional Networks:Visualising Image Classification Models and Saliency Maps](https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6034).
- [Original MNIST dataset description](https://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/).
